+// The same holed cube with three of the four upper edges of the hole filleted.
+// Two fillets end at corners of the hole whose next edge is not filleted. Each
+// end lies in the plane of the next wall of the hole, which also holds the edge
+// between the fillet of the cube and the sphere of its corner: the wall is
+// extended up to the end of the fillet and bounded by that edge. Depending on
+// the side from which the faces at the corner were met, the fillet was cut by
